  "notes": "Surface derived 2026-07-26 from merged WHATWG Fetch PR #1931 and HTML PR #12513 plus W3C Navigation Timing. Expanded after independent review: the inventory now includes the internal fetch bookkeeping (request and response navigation timing allow values list), the append algorithm, the navigation TAO check algorithm, and the final-response cloning flow, alongside the Timing-Allow-Origin header and the three PerformanceNavigationTiming attributes. Exact conditional corrected: same-origin-only chains always expose; the no-referrer gate and the all-hops TAO rule engage only when the chain has cross-origin redirects, and then EVERY hop (same-origin included) must opt in. Wildcard semantics documented from the algorithm steps ('*' succeeds regardless of credentials; need not be sole member). redirectStart/redirectEnd general-property BCD cited from api/PerformanceResourceTiming.json. webstatus query resolves to the broader Baseline 'Navigation timing' feature \u2014 not evidence about this addition. Deliberately partial pending independent review; parent promotes only after acceptance."
}
